Reproduction attempt: 2026-05-03T03:22:00Z
Engineer: automated forensics run (fix/schema-text-body-guard branch)

Methodology
-----------
400 parallel probes, max-time 10s each:
  - 200 × GET https://sapphirealpha.xyz/healthz/
  - 200 × GET https://tho.sapphirealpha.xyz/healthz/

Results
-------
Bad bodies (missing leading `{"` or schema-text detected): 0 / 400

Target endpoint findings:
  sapphirealpha.xyz/healthz/  → Returns {"dataset":"sapphire","ok":true,"project":"tho-ai-agent","ts":"..."}
                                This is a SAPPHIRE PROXY LAYER, not the THO FastAPI app.
                                It has its own /healthz/ handler that never shows schema-text.

  tho.sapphirealpha.xyz/healthz/ → Returns correct THO healthz JSON with:
                                   status=ok, version=896ed72..., uptime_s=~9549, dependencies all configured
                                   Server was WARM (9549s uptime) — cold-start conditions cannot be reproduced
                                   from outside. All 200 probes returned valid JSON.

Conclusion
----------
Reproduction was NOT triggered because:
1. The target instance was warm (uptime ~2.65 hours at probe time).
2. The bug only manifests at cold-start / post-deploy concurrency spike.
3. No Cloud Run auth to force a fresh revision deploy.

The schema-text body bug is NOT reproducible under load on a warm instance.
It requires a fresh cold-start with concurrent in-flight requests during
Python module import + FastAPI app initialization.

Proxy layer note
----------------
sapphirealpha.xyz is a separate routing gateway (Sapphire layer) that proxies
to tho.sapphirealpha.xyz. The /healthz/ route on the gateway is handled by the
gateway itself and is always valid JSON. The bug can only originate from the
THO FastAPI app at tho.sapphirealpha.xyz (or the Cloud Run URL directly).

Trace IDs captured: NONE (no bad bodies)
